# Git on Windows checks files out with CRLF by default. Every source file in
# this repo is LF, GitHub Pages serves LF, and a checkout that flipped all
# ninety files to CRLF would show the whole site as modified on the next
# machine that touched it. Store LF, check out LF, everywhere.
#
# text=auto still lets git sniff binaries, so the PNGs, the PDFs and the .ico
# are left alone.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Belt and braces for the ones that must never be touched.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.pdf  binary
*.ico  binary
*.svg  text eol=lf
